<title>USA: FMC awarded Canadian Terra Nova project.</title>
<headline>FMC awarded Canadian Terra Nova project.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>FMC Corp said its energy and transportation equipment group, through its participation in the Grand Banks Alliance, was selected to provide subsea and floating production equipment for Petro-Canada's Terra Nova oil field.</p>
<p>The field is offshore Newfoundland in Canada.</p>
<p>The sales value to FMC for the contract could total $230 million, it said.</p>
<p>The Grand Banks Alliance consists of FMC Offshore Canada Inc, an FMC subsidiary; ShawMont Brown and Root, a joint venture of ShawMont Newfoundland Ltd and Halliburton Co's Halliburton Canada Inc; Coflexip Stena Offshore International, PCL Industrial Contractors and DORIS Conpro Ltd.</p>
<p>		  ((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
